## Task File Management

```
tasks/active/YYYYMMDD_task-name.md    ← in-progress
tasks/done/YYYYMMDD_task-name.md      ← completed
tasks/_template.md                    ← copy to start
```

States: `[ ]` pending · `[~]` in progress · `[x]` done

Move to `done/` only after **explicit user confirmation** — never autonomously.

---

## Secrets

**Never in tracked files** — not even in comments, not even "temporarily." Use `.env` (gitignored); document variable names in `.env.example`. Scan `git diff --cached` before every commit.

---

## Git Workflow

- Format: short imperative, lowercase (`add nginx config`, `fix ssh keychain`)
- Phase done: `Phase N: <deliverable>`
- Mid-task: `wip: <task-name> — <step>`
- Rules changed: `rules: <what changed>`
- If `CLAUDE.md` or `modules/*.md` changed: run `./scripts/sync-rules.sh` (regenerates all `.cursor/rules/`)
- Before committing: review `git diff --cached`
- **Never commit or push automatically** — only when the user explicitly requests it
- Confirm before any destructive git operation (reset, force push, branch delete)
